export const mcpFaq = [
  ["How do I find where project audio is used?", "In My assets, audio rows show usage status and clickable application intervals. Click a range to select the clip and seek to its start; nested audio opens its owning composition first. Used audio omits duplicate file duration, and narrow panels keep usage on its own line. Detailed previews retain audition and visualization."],
  ['Can I generate from a reference image?', "Yes. Supported image models can edit a reference. OpenDesign Cloud and account video models with first-frame support can animate one image from Assets; Seedance 2.5 and Wan 2.7 use the image's aspect ratio. Prepare the reference first for a fixed frame. OpenDesign reference images must be under 2 MiB (other local adapters allow up to 20 MB)."],
  ['Which audio can I generate?', 'Speech, music and sound effects depend on the selected model and provider. BGM uses a music model. Use the discovered model mode and native parameters; an audio connection does not imply support for every audio operation.'],
  ['How is a Brand Kit different from a Template?', 'Open Brand Kit in Studio to extract a public website or choose the official collection, review its styles and download a Motion Package. Copy for Agent provides a local package path and style-only instructions. Reuse colors, typography, logos, component variants, materials and visual brand rules; context files travel with the package. The fixed showcase does not define your film’s pacing or story. For Agent access, use openmotion_assets_use with action=brand_kit. Brand Kits are separate from the MCP template catalogue.'],
  ["Can Studio run inside DeepSeek Harness?", "Yes, with the optional source-checkout workspace plugin for DSH 0.2.2-rc.1. Run the source-checkout DSH installer with the current profile and data directory, or use a verified release tarball. Refresh the browser if the new frontend is missing; do not restart the active conversation. The plugin opens the template library or Studio to the right of Agent chat and connects MCP to the same data. Configure your model in DSH; refresh the workspace to select newly created projects. This plugin is separate from the standard npm application."],
  ['Can I continue with another Agent?', 'Yes. Connect a compatible Agent to the same workspace and ask it to read the saved project before editing. Projects and assets can be reused; provide any conversation context it needs separately.'],
  ['Which Agents are supported?', 'Use Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, DeepSeek Harness or a desktop client that supports local stdio MCP. Choose your client above for the configuration for this installation. A configured server still needs to be verified inside the Agent.'],
  ['How do I reuse a community example?', exploreTemplateWorkflow],
  ['How do I use a Cinema Studio template?', 'Open Cinema Studio and select a template. Review the prompt and available model and settings. Add a first frame if requested, then select Generate.'],
  ['How can my Agent find short-form videos?', 'Call openmotion_list_templates and filter its index for shortForm=true. Open a matching work with openmotion_get_template. The Short-form video collection in Explore shows matching works with covers.'],
  ['How do I start with a scene or an editing preset?', 'Open Explore to choose a scene, preview an editable template or open an editing Skill. The Video menu also links to storyboards, scripted cuts and vertical shorts. Open a Skill, set its options and copy its instruction into your connected Agent.'],
  ['How do I start from a template?', 'Preview a template and send its prompt to your connected Agent. Ready-to-edit templates can be adapted or exported unchanged as an HTML project and MP4, with the exported file checked. Reference-only entries need reconstruction.'],
  ['Can I generate images, video, music and voice in one project?', 'Yes, when your configured providers support those media types. Ask the Agent to inspect the available models, generate the assets and arrange them in your project. Results are saved to local Assets and the original project paths. If local saving fails, open the task and choose Retry saving; this does not request generation again. Each model has its own inputs, limits and pricing.'],
  ['How long does a video take?', 'It depends on the film, the Agent, the selected models and your computer. Generation queues and rendering have separate progress. Keep following the existing job instead of submitting the same request again.'],
  ['Will my Agent use another video platform?', 'Your Agent chooses material sources to fit the content: real events call for original material; original visuals may use generation. It prefers OpenMotion when its available capabilities fit the operation, and can use other tools, including video platforms, to fill capability gaps. Your existing permissions and source preferences still apply.'],
  ['Can a team work on the same project?', 'Use All projects to export one project, checked projects or all projects as ZIP files. Import projects creates independent copies with local assets and fonts. Cloud collaboration, conversation history and provider credentials are not included. Linked online resources still need the internet.'],
  ['Does platform export publish my video?', 'No. Configure ASR in Model providers and review speech in Transcript. Your Agent creates editable platform and subtitle-language copies, previews them and exports files. You upload the finished files yourself.'],
  ['Who makes OpenMotion?', 'OpenMotion is an independent open-source project. The supported Agent and model names identify integrations, not ownership or endorsement. Visit the repository for the source, licenses and contribution guide.'],

  ['Do I need an OpenMotion API key?', 'Local MCP setup does not require an OpenMotion API key. Cloud generation uses your configured provider credentials or OpenDesign account. Keep keys in Model providers, not in chat.'],
  ['Which models can I use?', 'Available models come from your configured providers and account. Image, video, music and speech support depends on the selected model. Studio and MCP share model-specific parameters; available controls follow the selected model. A connected provider does not guarantee quota or generation success.'],
  ['Why can Codex chat work while image generation fails?', 'Codex login and image-service access are separate checks. For authorization errors, check the active Codex provider, endpoint and credentials. A proxy reporting a missing personal engine key needs its configured provider authentication; signing in again alone does not fix that configuration. Failed tasks preserve the original assets and are never retried automatically.'],
  ['How do I restore an asset version?', 'Open the asset, select a version in the right inspector and choose Make current version. Later versions remain available. Studio and MCP use the same asset update operation; references and downloads keep their exact version identity.'],
  ['Can ChatGPT cloud connect to this workspace?', 'This installation exposes local stdio, not a public HTTPS MCP endpoint. Use a local Agent or compatible desktop MCP client. The editor URL is not an MCP server URL.'],
  ['Can I recreate a reference video?', 'Yes. Give your Agent the reference and your brand. The recreation Skill analyses the reference, rebuilds the film as editable source and checks representative preview moments once, corrects clear defects in one batch and hands it over after automatic technical export verification. Detailed comparisons and further visual revisions run when requested. The Skill bundles reusable complete-texture and sprite-particle rendering code for editable projects. Optional source-observation and motion-measurement tools prepare their pinned Python, NumPy and OpenCV environment automatically on supported Macs and Windows PCs. First use needs network access unless the complete package includes the assets. Access to the reference, media understanding and fidelity depend on the host and supplied material.'],
  ['Where do I find my finished work?', 'Projects, source files, assets and versions stay in your local OpenMotion workspace. Open the project in Studio or ask a connected Agent to read it and continue. Completed exports provide the MP4.'],
  ['Can I see templates and videos inside my Agent?', 'Clients that negotiate MCP Apps can discover optional template cards and the final-video player. Codex installation shows the welcome followed by three randomly selected project-preview cards in a self-contained HTML document. Complete silent project previews and posters are bundled; this display does not wait for native MCP reload. Native original-reference playback remains available separately and needs internet access. Presentation and automatic MCP activation have separate acceptance: visible cards do not prove automatic activation. Preparation does not verify connection or visible delivery. Other clients use the local library, editor and video links; host support varies.'],
  ['How do I review a storyboard or creative direction?', 'Ask your Agent for a storyboard or direction options. Codex chats with inline HTML support can show expandable image cards. Other chats can show the images in order. Reply in chat with your choice or feedback. Use a playable sample to review motion and timing.'],
  ['What if the final video cannot load?', 'Prefer the host’s video preview; Codex normally shows it in the final reply. Use the OpenMotion player only if native preview is unavailable, never both for the same video. If the OpenMotion player cannot load, choose Reload to read the same completed export without rendering again.'],
  ['How do I disconnect an Agent?', 'Remove the OpenMotion MCP entry or plugin in that Agent. This does not delete projects. Remove provider credentials separately in Model providers if you no longer want generation access.'],
  ['Does connecting start generation or spend credits?', 'No. Copying setup instructions, browsing templates and checking a connection do not start media generation. Provider requests may incur charges; ask your Agent to confirm the model, scope and cost first.'],
  ['Can I transcribe recordings and make multilingual platform videos?', 'Yes. Open Captions → Auto captions to recognize video or audio directly, Add captions to type or paste subtitles, or import SRT/VTT without a model. The timeline T icon opens Add captions; creation selects the new track and opens Style. Existing managed text remains editable in the same panel. The timeline music icon imports audio, and the microphone records locally at the playhead. Transcribe with a configured speech model, review the text, then open Captions to choose a style and add captions to the video. Existing caption style, position and size changes apply immediately while preserving cue edits. The timeline CC menu opens recognition, manual creation or the chosen track’s styles and controls visibility. Use Translate or create versions to select a goal, platforms and subtitle languages, then copy an Agent brief with the exact project and transcript. Defaults use highlights, one platform and the source language; source links and custom choices are under More options. The Agent can retrieve supported links, inspect pictures, translate timed captions and create independent versions through MCP. Link retrieval and visual understanding depend on the host; subtitle translation keeps the original voice. Exports are files, not automatic platform publishing.'],
  ['How does Design Studio work with external Agents?', 'Design Studio manages HTML projects (prototypes, slide decks, documents, website clones, live artifacts and WebGL scenes), previews Desktop/Tablet/Mobile viewports, records annotations and versions, and exports ZIP, Open Design archives, standalone HTML, PDF, PNG and PPTX. OpenMotion runs no internal design agent: copy a brief or open annotations to Codex, Claude Code or any local MCP Agent, which calls openmotion_design_catalog, openmotion_design_project, openmotion_design_edit and openmotion_design_comments while Design Studio refreshes automatically.'],
  ['How does my Agent run a workflow and save results to Assets?', 'In Agent mode inside any workflow, fill in your task and click Copy for Agent to copy concise metadata, step-grouped Skills, and Assets references into your Agent; or switch to Step-by-step mode and click Copy MCP prompt on any step. Your Agent loads each library Skill with openmotion_get_skill (and workflow guides via openmotion://workflow/*), generates media directly (action=scenario, command=generate + sync), saves workspace assets into Assets and step history (command=add_pool with recordIteration=true), or links Design pages (command=link_design) and Motion projects (command=link_motion). Click Sync or return to Studio to see new deliverables immediately in Assets.'],
] as const;

